  "arrangerNotes": "Main theme = the first violin's opening entries (canon phrases A, B and C), verified against the Wikipedia LilyPond score. The later, faster variations go above the drum range and are left out. D drum: at score pitch (high 1 to 3 at the top), D minLayout 13. C drum: the C drum has no high 2 or 3, so the first phrase and the first half of the second (8 + 4 notes) are played one octave lower. The last four notes (4 3 4 2) stay at pitch because the C drum has no low 3 or 4. C minLayout 11. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum).",
  "verified": true
